{"id":"4d1a8a4f021bcbf6","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-lovaszmodularity.md","title":"Lovász concavity and convexity characterize modularity signs","display":"thm-lovaszmodularity — Lovász concavity and convexity characterize modularity signs","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-lovaszmodularity","aliases":["27-thm-lovaszmodularity"],"display":"thm-lovaszmodularity — Lovász concavity and convexity characterize modularity signs","depends_on":["[[27-df-submodular]]","[[27-thm-lovaszchainformula]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_section":"§13.6.3","source_statement":"Theorem 13.23, Equations (13.60)–(13.61)","source_printed_pages":"601–603","source_pdf_pages":"625–627","verification_status":"source-statement-and-proof-checked","local_review_status":"formalization-audited-from-supplied-text; source-not-rechecked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-lovaszmodularity"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-lovaszmodularity</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-lovaszmodularity — Lovász concavity and convexity characterize modularity signs"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"9c7a7ba711a14913\" href=\"?note=9c7a7ba711a14913\" title=\"27-df-submodular\">27-df-submodular</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"8749982edf417a9c\" href=\"?note=8749982edf417a9c\" title=\"27-thm-lovaszchainformula\">27-thm-lovaszchainformula</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§13.6.3"},{"key":"source_statement","html":"Theorem 13.23, Equations (13.60)–(13.61)"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"601–603"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"625–627"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-and-proof-checked"},{"key":"local_review_status","html":"formalization-audited-from-supplied-text; source-not-rechecked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in\\mathrm{PseudoBool}_n\">\\(f\\in\\mathrm{PseudoBool}_n\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f(\\chi_\\varnothing)=0\">\\(f(\\chi_\\varnothing)=0\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n,\\mathrm{Submodular}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n,\\mathrm{Submodular}_n\\)</span>（see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"9c7a7ba711a14913\" href=\"?note=9c7a7ba711a14913\" title=\"27-df-submodular\">27-df-submodular</a>），<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LovExt},S_\\pi,E_{\\pi,k},\\mathrm{Perm}(N)\">\\(\\mathrm{LovExt},S_\\pi,E_{\\pi,k},\\mathrm{Perm}(N)\\)</span>（see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8749982edf417a9c\" href=\"?note=8749982edf417a9c\" title=\"27-thm-lovaszchainformula\">27-thm-lovaszchainformula</a>），<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Concave}_n,\\mathrm{Convex}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Concave}_n,\\mathrm{Convex}_n\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"53f1b3025ce14af2\" href=\"?note=53f1b3025ce14af2\" title=\"27-df-pbextension\">27-df-pbextension</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)\\in\\mathrm{Concave}_n\\right)\\land\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Submodular}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)\\in\\mathrm{Convex}_n\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)\\in\\mathrm{Concave}_n\\right)\\land\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Submodular}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)\\in\\mathrm{Convex}_n\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Theorem 13.23 的陈述及印601–603/PDF625–627证明已核对，包括目视检查核心不等式。若 LovExt 凹，对顶点 x,y 使用中点凹性；x∧y、x∨y 在同一排序 simplex 内且和等于 x+y，故链仿射性给 supermodular 不等式。反向，把每个排列的链仿射式延至整个实空间；相邻逆序交换的差为正的坐标差乘 supermodular 四点差，故交换不会增加该式。按逆序数严格递减，至多 n(n−1)/2 次排序后得到 LovExt 是有限个仿射式的点式最小值，因而凹。原书末段写“at most n times”不足以界定全部相邻交换；本论证使用严格下降的逆序数。submodular/convex 结论对 −f 推出。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-submodular","status":"resolved","id":"9c7a7ba711a14913","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-submodular]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-thm-lovaszchainformula","status":"resolved","id":"8749982edf417a9c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-thm-lovaszchainformula]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-submodular","status":"resolved","id":"9c7a7ba711a14913","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$，$f\\in\\mathrm{PseudoBool}_n$，$f(\\chi_\\varnothing)=0$；$\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n,\\mathrm{Submodular}_n$（see [[27-df-submodular]]），$\\mathrm{LovExt},S_\\pi,E_{\\pi,k},\\mathrm{Perm}(N)$（see [[27-thm-lovaszchainformula]]），$\\mathrm{Concave}_n,\\mathrm{Convex}_n$ 见 [[27-df-pbextension]]。","embed":false},{"target":"27-thm-lovaszchainformula","status":"resolved","id":"8749982edf417a9c","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$，$f\\in\\mathrm{PseudoBool}_n$，$f(\\chi_\\varnothing)=0$；$\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n,\\mathrm{Submodular}_n$（see [[27-df-submodular]]），$\\mathrm{LovExt},S_\\pi,E_{\\pi,k},\\mathrm{Perm}(N)$（see [[27-thm-lovaszchainformula]]），$\\mathrm{Concave}_n,\\mathrm{Convex}_n$ 见 [[27-df-pbextension]]。","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-pbextension","status":"resolved","id":"53f1b3025ce14af2","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$，$f\\in\\mathrm{PseudoBool}_n$，$f(\\chi_\\varnothing)=0$；$\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n,\\mathrm{Submodular}_n$（see [[27-df-submodular]]），$\\mathrm{LovExt},S_\\pi,E_{\\pi,k},\\mathrm{Perm}(N)$（see [[27-thm-lovaszchainformula]]），$\\mathrm{Concave}_n,\\mathrm{Convex}_n$ 见 [[27-df-pbextension]]。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"f\\in\\mathrm{PseudoBool}_n","display":false},{"tex":"f(\\chi_\\varnothing)=0","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n,\\mathrm{Submodular}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LovExt},S_\\pi,E_{\\pi,k},\\mathrm{Perm}(N)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Concave}_n,\\mathrm{Convex}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Supermodular}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)\\in\\mathrm{Concave}_n\\right)\\land\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Submodular}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)\\in\\mathrm{Convex}_n\\right).","display":true}],"bytes":2210,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-454","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-lovaszmodularity|thm-lovaszmodularity — Lovász concavity and convexity characterize modularity signs]]"}],"outgoing":["9c7a7ba711a14913","8749982edf417a9c","53f1b3025ce14af2"]}